This distribution contains a narrow SGLang device-kernel fragment.
Origin: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
Revision: 06992c92ad4494fe9f9636e75be3e35040512447
Licensed under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE. HYLE adaptations isolate the
namespace and support macro and omit unrelated host glue. The original
activation arithmetic and packed indexing are retained.

C1-AB additionally extracts the pinned RMSNorm warp/CTA/double-load bodies
and norm/tile helpers, retaining their algorithm and reduction order. Host
binding and primitive CUDA shims replace TVM/Python glue; the Blackwell-only
32-byte path is not included. The Unary kernel shell uses an explicitly
adapted stable-tail formula and -infinity limiting value for HYLE's ordinary
Unary contract. Unary input/output restrict qualifiers are removed to permit
the documented exact in-place alias. See provenance.json for source hashes.
